      "title": "Session cookies are never marked Secure, even on HTTPS deployments",
      "technical_explanation": "The advanced.useSecureCookies=false setting is unconditional. The comment explains it exists to support plain-HTTP LAN deployments, but when an operator sets APP_URL to an https origin, the session cookie is still sent without the Secure flag, so it could be transmitted over an unencrypted connection if the browser is directed to an http URL for the same host. This is a hardening gap rather than demonstrated exposure, and it matches the project's documented plain-HTTP self-hosting use case.",
      "layman_explanation": "The login cookie is never marked as 'secure only', so on setups where the app is accessed over an encrypted connection, the cookie could still travel over an unencrypted one in some situations. This is a small safety gap, not an active problem for typical local use.",
      "developer_action": "Consider deriving the Secure cookie behavior from the APP_URL scheme (Secure when the configured origin uses https) instead of disabling it unconditionally, so HTTPS deployments get hardened cookies while plain-HTTP LAN use keeps working.",
      "locations": [
        {
